# Decisions

Record choices that later agents should not silently reverse. Newest first.

## 2026-09-20 — LAN browser test via `dev:lan`

- **Decision:** `npm run dev:lan` (`scripts/dev-lan.mjs`) auto-detects the host IPv4, binds Next (3010) and Nest (4010) on `0.0.0.0`, sets `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://<LAN_IP>:4010` and adds that origin to `WEB_ORIGIN`. Documented in `TESTING.md`. Do not disable the firewall; document `ufw allow` instead.
- **Why:** The Windows PC browser is not on this VM. `localhost` in `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` makes the PC call itself, not the worker.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Hardcoding 192.168.0.212 in source; opening CORS to `*`; disabling ufw.
- **Revisit when:** a public URL or Tailscale-only access is the default.

## 2026-09-20 — Per-account theme color (ADMIN)

- **Decision:** Store `User.themeColor` (`#rrggbb`, default `#3dcf8e`). ADMIN writes it only at `PATCH /users/:id/theme`. The web client sets `--theme` / `--theme-strong` on `<html>` so Tailwind `court-400`/`court-600` recolor every module. No dark-mode overhaul.
- **Why:** User asked for a simple per-account color wheel that is global across modules. A generic user PATCH would reopen the dues escalation hole.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Club-wide single theme; self-serve theme editor; new design system.
- **Revisit when:** the club wants a shared brand color instead of per-account accents.

## 2026-09-20 — Remaining Setup.md modules in one local product

- **Decision:** Ship iCal, announcements, coach notes, `archiveSeason`, ADMIN-only dues, plus team/roster/game-create so the club is demoable locally. Redis, Stripe, Storybook, and public signup stay out.
- **Why:** User asked to build the whole remaining stack and test after. Setup.md names these modules; it does not require a payment processor or cached season id.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Stopping after volunteer; adding Stripe for dues; Redis `activeSeasonId`; self-serve register.
- **Revisit when:** A processor or production host is named.

## 2026-09-20 — iCal feed is public (no JWT)

- **Decision:** `GET /calendar/teams/:teamId/feed.ics` is unauthenticated so Google Calendar can subscribe. Times are UTC `YYYYMMDDThhmmssZ` with `TZID:UTC`.
- **Why:** Calendar clients cannot send the httpOnly cookie. Team ids are UUIDs; the feed is schedule-only (no notes, dues, or emails).
- **Alternatives rejected:** JWT-gated .ics (breaks subscribe); local TZID without Z.
- **Revisit when:** the club wants signed/secret feed URLs.

## 2026-09-20 — Volunteer module (capacity lock)

- **Decision:** Isolated `VolunteeringModule`. ADMIN creates slots; PARENT registers; other roles list only. Capacity is `SELECT … FOR UPDATE` + recount, then insert; HTTP 409 when full or unique `(userId, slotId)` conflicts. Additive `seasonId` on `VolunteerSlot` so lists default to the active season (Setup.md model had no season).
- **Why:** Setup.md names ADMIN for volunteer setup and PARENT for signup. Event-style counts, not `capacity = capacity - 1`. Season leakage was already a documented failure mode.
- **Alternatives rejected:** COACH creating slots (not in Setup.md); PLAYER signup; check-then-insert without a lock; skipping seasonId.
- **Revisit when:** volunteer slots should attach to a specific Game.

## 2026-09-20 — First-slice security review

```text
Data: emails, password hashes, names, roles, isDuesPaid, game stats (likely youth PII later).
Boundaries: browser → Nest (cookie/Bearer JWT) → Prisma/Postgres; Socket.io handshake JWT; no public register.
Attackers: anonymous emit, PLAYER writing stats, isDuesPaid self-edit (no generic PATCH exists), archived-season leak, stolen JWT.
```

- **Fixed / designed in:** event-insert stats; active-season default; JWT required on HTTP + socket; COACH/ADMIN-only POST /stats; class-validator allowlists; parameterized Prisma; explicit CORS; login failures logged without email; httpOnly SameSite=Lax cookie; login 80/min/IP throttle (raised so `npm run smoke` can exercise every module).
- **Medium accepted:** no CSRF token (SameSite=Lax + credentialed API on another port); Next.js 14.2.25 still has an Image Optimizer advisory — `images.unoptimized` is on; no refresh-token denylist.
- **Open:** COPPA/consent before public launch; rotate `JWT_SECRET` playbook; Compose/host TLS.
- **Revisit when:** public URL or self-serve signup.

## 2026-09-20 — Embedded Postgres for Cloud smoke

- **Decision:** When Docker is missing, `scripts/dev-postgres.mjs` (`embedded-postgres`) serves local migrate/seed/smoke on port 5433. Compose remains the documented runtime.
- **Why:** First slice must be smokeable in Cloud Agents that have no Docker daemon.
- **Alternatives rejected:** SQLite (Setup.md requires Postgres); skipping smoke.
- **Revisit when:** Docker is the only supported path.

## 2026-09-20 — Volleyball Manager from Setup.md

- **Decision:** First product is **Volleyball Manager**. Stack is Next.js App Router + Tailwind, NestJS, PostgreSQL + Prisma, Socket.io, npm workspaces, Docker Compose. Repo root stays `Cursor_Forge`; layout is `apps/web-client`, `apps/api-server`, `packages/{database,shared-types,ui-components}`.
- **Why:** `Setup.md` named this stack and DDD monorepo. Golden path (Next + shadcn + Vercel) is opt-in only when there is no preference.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Golden path; single Next app with route handlers instead of NestJS; hosted Neon/Supabase; Vercel as the first deploy target; nesting the tree under `/volleyball-manager`.
- **Revisit when:** Production host is chosen, or Setup.md is explicitly superseded.

## 2026-09-20 — First slice is live stats only

- **Decision:** First shippable slice is coach records a timestamped `Stat` event and a parent live board updates over Socket.io. Volunteer, iCal, announcements, coach notes, season archive UI, and payments stay out.
- **Why:** `scope-feature` — one demo moment. The blueprint is a full platform; shipping it at once hides whether realtime + RBAC + season scope work.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Scaffolding every module in Setup.md before a working path; Redis in v1; Stripe before a processor is named.
- **Revisit when:** First-slice checklist is green (`assets/checklists/first-slice.md`).

## 2026-09-20 — MCP: context7 + playwright only

- **Decision:** Enable `context7` (HTTP docs) and `playwright` (browser verify). No Vercel, Neon, Supabase, Stripe, or GitHub MCP.
- **Why:** Agents will look up Nest/Next/Prisma docs and smoke the coach/parent UI. Local Compose Postgres has no hosted-DB MCP. Dues are an ADMIN flag, not Stripe.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Enabling the whole catalog; Vercel MCP despite Docker-first deploy.
- **Revisit when:** A hosted DB, payment processor, or production PaaS is chosen.

## 2026-09-20 — Threat model (auth, PII, dues flag, public API)

```text
Data: account (email, passwordHash, name), Role, isDuesPaid (payment status, not card data), coach notes, volunteer signups, game stats; likely youth/minor PII.
Boundaries: browser → Next.js → NestJS → Postgres; Socket.io rooms; later public-ish iCal feed.
Attackers: authenticated parent/player escalating role or isDuesPaid; stolen JWT; anonymous socket emit; concurrent volunteer overbook; iCal scrape.
Blast radius: JWT_SECRET compromise = all sessions; DATABASE_URL = full club PII including minors; one COACH can write notes on rostered players.
Logging: auth failures, role/dues changes, volunteer 409s. Never passwords, tokens, note bodies, or raw emails.
Recovery: rotate JWT_SECRET and force re-login; Postgres restore from Compose volume/backup (runbook not written). Open: no refresh-token revocation list.
Open risks: COPPA/parental consent before public launch; no payment processor; no key-rotation playbook; iCal caching/timezone; Redis not in v1 so active season is a DB read.
```

- **Guardrails from Setup.md:** event-sourced stats; default active-season queries; volunteer transaction + lock (409); UTC `scheduledAt`; `isDuesPaid` ADMIN-only endpoint.
- **Revisit when:** public deploy, payments, or self-serve signup ships — run `security-review`.

## 2026-09-19 — First product on a dedicated branch

- **Decision:** First product bootstrap happens on `cursor/start-new-app-b09f`, leaving `main` as the blank starter until the app is real.
- **Why:** User asked to familiarize, then start the app on a new branch. Product and stack are now named in the 2026-09-20 entries.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Scaffolding on `main` immediately; picking golden path without confirmation.
- **Revisit when:** First slice is merged to `main`.

## 2026-08-29 — Vibe coder capability layer

- **Decision:** Golden path (`assets/stack-playbooks/golden-path.md`) is **opt-in** when the user has no stack preference — not an automatic default.
- **Why:** Speed for vibe coding without trapping users who named a stack.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Golden path as hard default; stay fully silent with no opinionated option.
- **Revisit when:** Most clones pick the same stack in practice.

- **Decision:** Feature integrations use one `add-integration` skill plus `assets/recipes/*.md`, not six nearly identical skills.
- **Why:** One procedure; stack/vendor detail stays on-demand; Cloud Agents get portable recipes without user-level vendor skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** One skill per integration; relying only on `~/.cursor` vendor skills.
- **Revisit when:** A recipe grows large enough to need its own skill (migrations already did → `migrate-database`).

- **Decision:** UI polish is a `polish-ui` skill + `assets/checklists/ui-polish.md` (verifiable), with globbed `30-frontend.mdc` for local habits.
- **Why:** Vibe users judge on look/feel; always-apply must stay short.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Dumping a full style guide into always-apply rules.
- **Revisit when:** The product adopts a stricter design system.

## 2026-08-29 — Agent starter hardening

- **Decision:** Boilerplate (CI, GitHub templates, Docker, linters, hooks) stays under `assets/templates/` and is copied on demand — not materialized at repo root.
- **Why:** Keeps the starter stack-agnostic; Cloud and local clones stay blank until bootstrap.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Materializing CI/Docker at root; hybrid root+templates for every file.
- **Revisit when:** The starter itself becomes a product app, or users consistently want default CI at clone time.

- **Decision:** Security is both prose and tooling — `security-review` skill, `security-reviewer` subagent, `20-security.mdc`, checklists, `scripts/scan-secrets.mjs`, and a CI security-scan template.
- **Why:** Agents need a planned review path and a mechanical gate; Cloud Agents cannot rely on user-level security skills.
- **Alternatives rejected:** Checklist-only; tooling-only without a review runbook.
- **Revisit when:** A preferred org-wide scanner replaces the local script.

- **Decision:** Cursor hooks ship as inert templates under `assets/templates/hooks/` (Node `.mjs`), not enabled by default.
- **Why:** Hooks change every agent run; a bad deny rule blocks work. Node scripts are portable to Windows and Linux Cloud Agents (`.sh` is not).
- **Alternatives rejected:** Activating `.cursor/hooks.json` out of the box; shell-only hooks.
- **Revisit when:** The user asks to enable project hooks.

## Template defaults (2026-08-29)

- **Working memory lives in project rules**, not chat and not `~/.cursor`. Cloud Agents only see the repo.
- **Skills for workflows, rules for constraints.** Bootstrap, MCP, and memory updates are skills.
- **MCP is opt-in.** The catalog is in `assets/mcp-catalog.md`. `.cursor/mcp.json` starts empty.
- **No application stack until bootstrap.** Do not assume Next.js, Python, or any framework.

